  {
    "name": "Information and Rumour Table",
    "folder": "Non-player Characters",
    "formula": "1d6",
    "description": "<p>p.57. First determine the NPC’s reaction, then roll D3 for the number of pieces of information they share. Roll 1D for the type of each piece, then roll the listed die (or use the matching Information sub-table).</p>",
    "results": [
      {
        "range": [
          1,
          1
        ],
        "text": "<strong>Adventure Lead:</strong> Roll 1D; 1) Person; 2) Place; 3) Thing; 4) Object; 5) Background info; 6) Secret. <em>This information leads to potential side jobs or personal interest pursuits.</em>"
      },
      {
        "range": [
          2,
          2
        ],
        "text": "<strong>Narrative Information:</strong> Roll 1D; 1) Major fact; 2) Minor fact; 3) Notable fact; 4) Unnecessary fact; 5) Valuable information; 6) Unexpected connection. <em>This information assists or advances the spacer’s current narrative.</em>"
      },
      {
        "range": [
          3,
          3
        ],
        "text": "<strong>Job Information:</strong> Roll D3; 1) Fact about patron; 2) Fact about a place; 3) Fact about a job detail. <em>Any information that assists the spacer with their current job they may have questions about.</em>"
      },
      {
        "range": [
          4,
          4
        ],
        "text": "<strong>Job Lead:</strong> Roll 1D; 1) Patron suggestion; 2) Job rumour; 3) Criminal patron suggestion; 4) Criminal job rumour; 5) Secret patron suggestion; 6) Secretive job rumour. <em>This information can lead a spacer to a potential client or a rumoured job a patron is offering.</em>"
      },
      {
        "range": [
          5,
          5
        ],
        "text": "<strong>Rumour:</strong> Roll 1D; 1) NPC connection; 2) Faction Connection; 3) Location connection; 4) Narrative clue; 5) Adventure clue; 6) Job clue. <em>Rumours require additional roleplaying to discern the source of the rumour or if the information offered is actionable. Use the Discernment table to determine the truth of the rumours.</em>"
      },
      {
        "range": [
          6,
          6
        ],
        "text": "<strong>Local Gossip:</strong> Roll 1D; 1) Illicit information on an NPC; 2) Illicit info on a faction; 3) Illicit info on a location; 4) Dangerous information; 5) Conspiracy theory; 6) Unbelievable connection. <em>Gossip is information that NPCs will share that is open-ended and may not be related to a current objective. It is essentially local flavour that may be actionable if the spacer decided to pursue it.</em>"
      }
    ]
